# 4. How it works & accessibility notes
- **Pin:** the thumbtack button in `AppsSection` toggles `ui.pinnedProjects` (ids) — persisted automatically by `saveState()`/`loadState()`.
- **Switch:** `PinnedProjectsSwitcher` calls `$projects.activeProjectChanged(project)`, reusing the existing loading overlay, chat reload and route-prefix sync.
- **Accessibility:** native `<button>`s, `aria-pressed` + `aria-label` on the pin toggle, `title` tooltips on each pinned item, visible focus rings (`focus-visible:ring-2 ring-primary/50`), and the "unpin" action is a separate focusable control (not color-only).
- **Anti-patterns avoided:** only ids are persisted (no stale project snapshots); the switcher is hidden when empty (no empty-shell UI); no custom CSS/colors beyond the existing design tokens (`bg-primary/15`, `border-base-content/5`, etc.).

**Try it:** open a project → click the thumbtack next to the project selector → the project appears under **PINNED** at the top of the sidebar → open another project, pin it → click any pinned item to jump back instantly.

